"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liao</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ali</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Greene</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Muller</surname><given-names>W.A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Soluble domain 1 of platelet-endothelial cell adhesion molecule (PECAM) is sufficient to block transendothelial migration in vitro and in vivo</article-title><source>J. Exp. Med.</source><volume>185</volume><year>1997</year><fpage>1349</fpage><lpage>1357</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9104821</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Limetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lim</surname><given-names>Y.-C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Snapp</surname><given-names>K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kansas</surname><given-names>G.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Camphausen</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ding</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Luscinskas</surname><given-names>F.W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Important contributions of P-selectin glycoprotein ligand-1&#x02013;mediated secondary capture to human monocyte adhesion to P-selectin, E-selectin, and TNF-&#x003b1;&#x02013;activated endothelium under flow in vitro</article-title><source>J. Immunol.</source><volume>161</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>2501</fpage><lpage>2508</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9725249</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Lorenzonetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lorenzon</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Vecile</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Nardon</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ferrero</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Harlan</surname><given-names>J.M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tedesco</surname><given-names>F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dobrina</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Endothelial cell E- and P-selectin and vascular cell adhesion molecule-1 function as signaling receptors</article-title><source>J. Cell Biol.</source><volume>142</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>1381</fpage><lpage>1391</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9732297</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Luscinskasetal1989"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luscinskas</surname><given-names>F.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Brock</surname><given-names>A.F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnaout</surname><given-names>M.A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gimbrone</surname><given-names>M.A.</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Endothelial-leukocyte adhesion molecule-1 (ELAM-1)&#x02013;dependent and leukocyte (CD11/CD18)-dependent mechanisms contribute to polymorphonuclear leukocyte adhesion to cytokine-activated human vascular endothelium</article-title><source>J. Immunol.</source><volume>142</volume><year>1989</year><fpage>2257</fpage><lpage>2263</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2564407</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Luscinskasetal1994"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luscinskas</surname><given-names>F.W.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kansas</surname><given-names>G.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ding</surname><given-names>H.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pizcueta</surname><given-names>P.</given-names></name><name><surname>Schleiffenbaum</surname><given-names>B.E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Tedder</surname><given-names>T.F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gimbrone</surname><given-names>M.A.</given-names><suffix>Jr.</suffix></name></person-group><article-title>Mon